course: dictionary
lesson: 9021
title: Animal defences: the skunk
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some animals protect themselves by warning enemies before they attack. Context helps you understand this word. «A skunk can spray a very smelly liquid up to about 3 metres, but it usually warns first by stamping, hissing and raising its tail.» The words warns and first tell you the skunk gives a signal before it sprays.
explain: A skunk is a noun. You can say a skunk or two skunks. It is a small black-and-white animal with a bushy tail, and it lives in North America. When it is frightened, it sprays a very bad-smelling liquid.
explain: Some animals hide, but others want to be seen. «The bright blue poison dart frog and the black and white skunk wear warning colours that say, loud and clear, do not even try.» The stripes are a warning, not a hiding place. Swap your meaning into the sentence to check that it still makes sense.
fact: A skunk is a small black-and-white animal with a bushy tail, from North America.
fact: «Skunk» is a noun: one skunk, two skunks.
fact: To «spray» means to shoot a liquid out in a fine mist, and a skunk sprays a very smelly liquid.
fact: A skunk usually warns first by stamping, hissing and raising its tail.
fact: The phrase «smell like a skunk» means to smell very bad.
exercise: «A skunk can spray a very smelly liquid, but it usually warns first.» What is a skunk? | A loud type of drum | A bird that sings at night | A tree with black bark | *A small black-and-white animal with a bushy tail
exercise: Skunks «warn first by stamping, hissing and raising the tail.» What does warn mean here? | Run very fast away | Hide from others forever | *Give a clear signal that danger may come | Wash your face
exercise: «Real skunks are fairly calm and spray only as a last resort.» What does calm mean? | *Relaxed and not easily upset | Angry and ready to fight | Hungry | Very loud
test: «Refilling the spray takes days.» What does this tell you about a skunk? | It never sprays at all | It sprays only at night | *It needs several days to make enough spray again | It can spray again every minute
test: Why are the skunk's black and white stripes useful? | To help it run faster | To hide it in the snow | To make it look like a tree | *To warn enemies to keep away
exam: Which word means to shoot a liquid out in a fine mist? | Stamp | Drip | *Spray | Hiss
